  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening malaria control in Benin - Benin (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Benin, Malaria, Programme National de Lutte contre le Paludisme de la R&#xe9;publique du B&#xe9;nin (PNLP)This program has the following goals: Achieve a mortality rate as close to zero as possible (one death per 100,000 inhabitants) for all avoidable malaria-related deaths by 2018.  Reduce the number of cases of malaria by 75 percent by 2015 (compared with 2000 levels of 12.72 percent) and maintain this level until 2018. The objectives of this program are: By the end of 2018, 100% of suspected malaria cases are given a biological/parasitological test, and correct treatment in public and private health facilities at Community level.  By the end of 2018, 100% of the population, including pregnant women and children under 5 sleep under insecticide-treated nets.  By the end of 2018, the management capacity of NMCP in the fight against malaria are strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
